  "scope": "D3D8/9 share identity/query cache, copied full WORD RGB ramp storage, flag storage and SET_GAMMA_RAMP encoding. D3D8 no longer drops setters or returns zero ramps and now advertises virtual full-screen gamma. NULL inputs remain no-ops; D3D9 retains its invalid-chain behavior. Gamma changes remain live during state-block recording. Void setters keep requested cache on transport failure and repeat calls emit again. Both actual Reset replay functions resend a supplied ramp with its flags under the new device handle and return failure if that submission fails. Real XP exercises sixteen clear/present frames, exact queries and live state blocks, two fullscreen/windowed-parameter Resets per API and identity restoration. The probe creates an exact 64x64 client area so final scanout matches the known back-buffer extent. Separate GPU replay checks all 65536 final scanout pixels plus all 65536 raw back-buffer pixels per backend; scanout uses the expected LUT and raw images retain the clear color. The host and bundle are unchanged, so the full stage4h6a GPU baseline is inherited with fresh gamma pages on both backends. Physical OS monitor calibration, gamma calibration flags, OS fullscreen style/mode/focus restoration, complete Reset/API/native Microsoft HAL/Wine/game/FPS behavior, cursor/private-data/pacing/surface-identity/additional-swapchain contracts and completed stages 4/5/6 are not claimed.",
